up (SPG). This chart runs from May 15, 2009 to Sep 22, 2009.","setup":"The stock rose about 140% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 9 weeks, peaking at $57.04 and pulling back 22% at its deepest. Daily price ranges stayed about the same width through the base.","outcome":"On Aug 4, 2009 it closed at $60.47, its first close above the base high of $56.92. Volume that day was 8.7M shares, 2.33x the prior 10-day average of 3.7M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $73.97, and the chart ends at $73.41.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}